1. The Langevin method for Markov chain Monte Carlo methods
There has recently been a real explosion in the use of the Hastings and Metropolis algorithms, which allow simulation of a probability density ~ ( xw) hich is known only up to a factor: that is, when only T ( x ) / T ( ~ )is known. This is especially relevant when T is the posterior distribution in a Bayesian context: see Besag and Green (1993), Besag et al. (1995), Mengersen and Tweedie (1996), Roberts and Tweedie (1996), Smith and Roberts (1993) and Tierney (1994) for a variety of approaches and properties of such methods, and their applications in statistical modelling.
